<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16046" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕpŭlor</span></b> ,
			ātus, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i> and <i>a.</i> [epulum], <i>to hold an entertainment</i>,
				<i>to feast</i>, <i>banquet.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut in voluptate sit, qui epuletur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 2, 5, 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. de Sen. 13, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc.
				1, 47, 113</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 5, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 42,
			56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">44, 31</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Tac. H.
				3, 38</span></i>.—With abl., <i>to feast upon</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3, 224</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. G. 2,
				537</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Deut. 12, 12
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to eat</i>, <i>feast upon</i> (not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem epulandum ponere mensis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 4, 602</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15, 111</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Troad. 1108</span></i>; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pullos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 43, 68, § 170</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
